{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_015PzYkGRvdfeDL8bE7qK7Aa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to define three tiers (best/median/worst) for a Dream simulation of their ContamCal-IRT calibration project. They want this based on the detailed research context provided. Let me analyze the key elements:\n\n1. The project is about contamination-calibrated IRT (4PL+γ) for benchmark evaluation\n2. Target venue: AAAI 2027\n3. Core claims: Calibration, Signal Aggregation, Uncertainty Quantification\n4. One experiment done (MVP simulation): γ rel_bias 6.8%, θ_corr 0.943, good convergence\n\n\n5. Key evaluation metrics include MAE, CI coverage and sharpness, Kendall's τ, and dose-response monotonicity\n\nFor the best case, all three core claims validate strongly—the 4PL+γ model recovers true scores with low MAE, RRF fusion clearly outperforms individual signals, and uncertainty quantification is well-calibrated with appropriate CI coverage. For the median case, calibration holds up in the SFT injection experiment but the RL observational study shows weaker results, perhaps with RRF not decisively beating the best single signal or mixed dose-response patterns.\n\nIn the worst case, identifiability breaks down on real data despite simulation success, with γ and θ becoming confounded and RRF exposure scores too noisy to be useful—though I could reframe this as a negative result about when IRT calibration actually works, or shift focus to the signal survival analysis as the main contribution. I need to pin down specific number ranges for MAE in percentage points, 95% CI coverage and width, Kendall's τ for ranking preservation, monotonicity patterns, RRF AUC, and the γ parameter estimates.\n\nNow I'm laying out realistic performance ranges across best and median scenarios—MAE targets from 1-3 pp up to 3-6 pp, CI coverage between 90-97% and 85-93%, Kendall's τ spanning 0.85-0.95 down to 0.70-0.85, with corresponding expectations for dose-response monotonicity, RRF AUC, and relative bias on real data.\n\nFor the worst case, I'm looking at substantially degraded metrics—MAE ballooning to 6-12 pp, CI coverage dropping to 75-85% with either excessive width or dangerous narrowness, Kendall's τ falling to 0.50-0.70, non-monotonic dose-response patterns, RRF AUC around 0.60-0.70, and relative bias exceeding 25% or minimal improvement over baselines. Now I'm thinking through how to frame the narrative for each performance tier.\n\nThe user's feedback is clear: the core assumptions don't hold, so I need to find a new angle to reframe this while keeping the same venue and ambition level. I'm considering several pivots—reframing it as an empirical study of when IRT calibration actually works and what identifiability conditions matter, elevating the signal survival analysis from a supporting contribution to the main story, positioning it as an investigation of the gap between simulation and reality in contamination calibration, or even leaning into a negative results narrative about why statistical contamination calibration is fundamentally harder than expected. Let me structure these reframe options more systematically.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10777,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10777},"output_tokens":26,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7cd974dd-bb19-4d39-a4ca-894d97bde4de","uuid":"bf0c8d3a-79f8-4f00-b6b3-7abdc8f33794"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_015PzYkGRvdfeDL8bE7qK7Aa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntiers:\n  best:\n    meaning: \"4PL+γ在真实SFT注入数据上完全复现仿真表现；RRF融合信号质量高；RL观测案例显示方向性有效且CIs合理宽化。三条claims原封不动成立。\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - SFT注入后检测信号AUC在真实数据上达到0.80+（与仿真设定匹配）\n      - γ与θ在真实数据上可识别（posterior correlation < 0.4，与MVP仿真一致）\n      - RRF融合明显优于任何单信号（ΔAUC ≥ 0.05）\n      - 4PL+γ显著优于所有5个baselines（MAE相对改善 > 30%）\n      - RL regime下Self-Critique仍提供AUC ≥ 0.70的信号，CIs合理宽化而非崩溃\n      - dose-response严格单调，跨4个benchmark一致\n    number_ranges:\n      calibration_mae_pp: [1.0, 3.0]\n      ci_coverage_95pct: [0.90, 0.97]\n      ci_width_95_pp: [4, 8]\n      kendall_tau: [0.85, 0.95]\n      dose_response_spearman: [0.90, 1.00]\n      rrf_exposure_auc: [0.80, 0.90]\n      gamma_rel_bias_real_data: [0.03, 0.10]\n      theta_corr_with_ground_truth: [0.92, 0.98]\n      margin_over_best_baseline_mae_relative: [0.30, 0.50]\n      rl_case_expected_regret_reduction: [0.25, 0.45]\n      two_signal_degraded_mae_increase_relative: [0.05, 0.15]\n    narrative_direction: >\n      原始framing完全成立：ContamCal是benchmark contamination的\"statistical safety net\"，\n      三条claims按原始强度表述。Headline: \"ContamCal recovers true performance within 2pp MAE\n      with 93% CI coverage, while naive scores overestimate by 8-12pp.\" \n      RL宽CI叙事自然成立——\"wide CIs are the correct answer\"用expected regret量化证明。\n      投AAAI无需调整framing。\n\n  median:\n    meaning: \"SFT regime下calibration有效但不如仿真理想；RRF优于单信号但优势不大；RL观测CIs过宽、expected regret改善有限。需要调整claims强度并补充实验。\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - 真实数据检测信号AUC在0.70-0.80区间（低于仿真最优设定）\n      - γ可识别但posterior与θ有中等相关（0.3-0.5），部分benchmark γ的95%CI接近包含0\n      - RRF优于最佳单信号但ΔAUC仅0.02-0.04\n      - 4PL+γ优于多数baselines但linear regression+CI在简单benchmark上接近\n      - dose-response大体单调但GSM8K或HumanEval出现1-2个非单调点\n      - RL regime下Self-Critique AUC ~0.60-0.65，CIs宽到15-20pp\n      - 7B scale结果与0.5-3B一致（无scale regression）\n    number_ranges:\n      calibration_mae_pp: [3.0, 6.0]\n      ci_coverage_95pct: [0.85, 0.93]\n      ci_width_95_pp: [8, 14]\n      kendall_tau: [0.70, 0.85]\n      dose_response_spearman: [0.75, 0.90]\n      rrf_exposure_auc: [0.70, 0.80]\n      gamma_rel_bias_real_data: [0.10, 0.20]\n      theta_corr_with_ground_truth: [0.82, 0.92]\n      margin_over_best_baseline_mae_relative: [0.10, 0.30]\n      rl_case_expected_regret_reduction: [0.08, 0.25]\n      two_signal_degraded_mae_increase_relative: [0.15, 0.35]\n    narrative_direction: >\n      Claims需要降级修饰。Claim 1加条件限定：\"在检测信号AUC≥0.70的SFT regime下有效校准\"，\n      不再claim跨regime通用性。Claim 2从\"outperforming any single signal\"弱化为\n      \"robust aggregation with graceful degradation\"，重心移向鲁棒性而非优越性。\n      Claim 3的RL部分从\"appropriately wider intervals\"改为诚实承认CIs过宽时的实用性边界，\n      用simulation identifiability bounds来定义\"minimum useful signal quality\"。\n      需要补充实验：(a) exp-011 few-examinee regime证明Growing Pains预估策略能改善小样本表现，\n      (b) exp-010 prior sensitivity证明结果非prior-driven。\n      论文叙事从\"general calibration framework\"调整为\"principled calibration under \n      sufficient signal quality, with explicit identifiability guarantees\"。\n      仍投AAAI，但方法论贡献权重从calibration accuracy转向identifiability analysis。\n\n  worst:\n    meaning: \"γ-θ在真实数据上严重混淆；RRF信号质量不足以支撑有意义的校准；4PL+γ未显著优于simple baselines。核心calibration claim不成立，需reframe。\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - 真实数据检测信号AUC < 0.70（信号质量低于仿真identifiability threshold）\n      - γ与θ posterior correlation > 0.5，γ的95%CI在多数条件下包含0\n      - RRF融合无显著优于单信号，甚至不如embedding retrieval单信号\n      - 4PL+γ与vanilla 4PL或linear regression在MAE上无统计显著差异\n      - dose-response非单调——低dosage（5%,25%）γ无法检出，仅100% dosage显著\n      - CI coverage严重偏离nominal（undercoverage < 80% 或 overcoverage因CIs过宽）\n      - RL regime下所有信号AUC < 0.60，calibration本质上不可行\n    number_ranges:\n      calibration_mae_pp: [6.0, 12.0]\n      ci_coverage_95pct: [0.70, 0.85]\n      ci_width_95_pp: [15, 25]\n      kendall_tau: [0.50, 0.70]\n      dose_response_spearman: [0.40, 0.75]\n      rrf_exposure_auc: [0.58, 0.70]\n      gamma_rel_bias_real_data: [0.25, 0.50]\n      theta_corr_with_ground_truth: [0.65, 0.82]\n      margin_over_best_baseline_mae_relative: [-0.10, 0.10]\n      rl_case_expected_regret_reduction: [-0.05, 0.10]\n      two_signal_degraded_mae_increase_relative: [0.35, 0.60]\n    narrative_direction: >\n      核心calibration claim不成立。Reframe方向（仍投AAAI）：\n      主线转为\"Empirical Identifiability Boundaries for Contamination-Aware IRT\"——\n      系统性研究在什么条件下（信号质量×模型数量×contamination强度）IRT校准才可行。\n      贡献重构：(1) 大规模仿真identifiability map（exp-004已完成，这成为Core Contribution 1），\n      (2) signal survival analysis升级为Core（exp-008，揭示检测信号在post-training后的脆弱性），\n      (3) controlled SFT注入作为empirical validation——证明仿真预测的identifiability边界\n      与真实数据吻合（\"仿真说AUC<0.70不行，真实数据confirm了\"）。\n      叙事逻辑：\"Before building calibration systems, we need to know when they can work. \n      We provide the first systematic identifiability analysis for contamination-augmented IRT, \n      revealing that current detection signals are insufficient for reliable calibration in \n      most practical settings — establishing concrete signal quality targets for future work.\"\n      这变成一篇diagnostic/negative-result+roadmap论文，仍有AAAI级贡献（方法论+实证），\n      但claims从\"we solve calibration\"变为\"we map when calibration is solvable\"。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10777,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10777},"output_tokens":26,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7cd974dd-bb19-4d39-a4ca-894d97bde4de","uuid":"6c13ff33-3e05-4d29-87bd-cad86377fd8f"}
